# Profile "realtime": 1 lab minute = 1 real minute (cloud run, real 01:00 / 10:00 JST).
# Delete-path pacing is scaled 1:200, the same ratio as the RPC capacity in docker-config,
# so a 30,000-key delete in the lab drains as long as a 6,000,000-key delete in production.
#   production default                          -> lab
#   ozone.key.deleting.limit.per.task 20000/run -> 100/run   (OM KeyDeletingService)
#   hdds.scm.block.deletion.per-interval.max 100000 -> 500   (SCM -> datanode delete commands)
#   hdds.datanode.block.deleting.limit.per.interval 5000 -> 25
OZONE-SITE.XML_ozone.key.deleting.limit.per.task=100
OZONE-SITE.XML_hdds.scm.block.deletion.per-interval.max=500
OZONE-SITE.XML_hdds.datanode.block.deleting.limit.per.interval=25
# SCM Ratis request timeout, scaled with the handler count (production 100 OM handlers x 30s;
# lab 5 handlers x 600s). When SCM Ratis stalls, SCM finishes about one block call per timeout;
# the scaling keeps the production ratio "waiting OM calls x timeout > OM->SCM timeout (15m)"
# that makes OM retries pile up in the SCM queue.
OZONE-SITE.XML_ozone.scm.ha.ratis.request.timeout=600s
